  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Wiki_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bfa36fdea331abe4cb2b293833ff63a0, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 188400156672
    m_Localized: Alter-Echo production has been retired. Gather resources on adventures or harvest planted crops.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 478381752320
    m_Localized: 'Buffs are short-term, timed powers that expire when they run out or if you return to town.  They can be autocast after completing the required quest for the slot and the autocasting defaults to on. You can toggle it off by clicking the slot in the buffs management window.


      Buff cooldowns can be reduced via Eva''s Cauldron.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 492340396032
    m_Localized: "Your character will enter combat automatically, and only engage enemies who get in the way! Tasks first fun later.\n\nD' = D \xD7 (1 - A / (A + N))\n\nD = incoming damage\nA = defense value (clamped to 0 or higher)\nN = constant scalar that controls diminishing returns (default = 25)\nD' = final damage taken\n\nReaching your 10th, 100th, 1,000th, and 10,000th kill against a specific enemy will grant you 25% bonus damage against that specific enemy.\nReaching your 25,000th, and 100,000th kill against a specific enemy will grant you 50% bonus damage against that specific enemy."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 512217202688
    m_Localized: "Echoes are alternate versions of your character who will shift slightly into their reality to help out under various circumstances.\n\nEach echo can have a combination of your character's skillset. But most Echoes won't have them all.\n\nThe main difference in Echo behaviour comes from whether or not they are combat enabled.\nCombat-enabled Echoes have two different styles depending on whether or not they can also complete tasks. \n\nA combat-enabled Echo that does NOT have the ability to do tasks will seek out enemies specifically.\nA combat-enabled Echo that DOES have the ability to do tasks will prioritize tasks over combat and only engage enemies that see them.\n\nEchoes that do not have combat will not be targeted by or target enemies.\n\nDev Note | Right now there are no echoes in the game that can do both combat and tasks. Echoes from Milestones specifically seek out tasks for that skills milestone EG an echo spawned with woodcutting will only seek out woodcutting tasks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 532437942272
    m_Localized: 'For each kill you get on a run, your resource bonus goes up by 2%. During combat, this is temporarily set to 0%


      Aim to retreat just before combat gets too tough for you to handle so that you get as many bonus resources as possible!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 698595295232
    m_Localized: 'Tasks are the primary purpose of your character''s journey. Gathering resources for the town is essential to growth.


      These are completed automatically, and you will complete them faster as your skills level.


      Task spawns have a range from minimum to maximum distance, however after reaching maximum distance their chance to spawn goes down by 90%. With this considered once all tasks are at their maximum the weight system will average out and all tasks will be equally available based on their weights.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 505754247643136
    m_Localized: 'Quests have different types of conditions that need to be met before you hand them in.


      <b>Information</b> | These quests are instantly completed, either for story, or to guide you through the intro.

      <b>Gathering</b> | These quests require you to gather resources and hand them in to complete.

      <b>Kills</b> | Kill enemies and report back to complete these.

      <b>Meet</b> | Require you to meet a certain NPC most of whom are found at specific distances reached.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3785742338113536
    m_Localized: "Upon reaching certain distances from the town Carl will reap your soul ensuring you don't stray too far. \nYou can view your maximum reaping distance in the statistics under the General Tab.\n\nReaping distance is increased via the following methods.\n<b>Being Reaped</b> | Increases distance by 1% of your current maximum reaping distance. (Except on farmlands)\n<b>Quests</b> | Some quests will provide a reaping distance increase."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6939642239008768
    m_Localized: v1.4.3
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7986628786536448
    m_Localized: 'Dragon slaying pope

      tanty.

      Mellifas

      Latimer Cross

      MatHeadGetz

      appleguy

      AwesomePhoenix

      boiledpotato

      eli

      GLUTTONY

      Gudu

      Mentocado

      Nuclearion

      Quackers

      Rugmuk

      SaintPlays

      SCHMUGGLER

      WaringMcMarrin'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133160779776
    m_Localized: "Ivan's forge is a magical place. Whether you're chilling in town or out on the road, you can help guide him as he improves his smithing skills.\n\nYou have access to two toggles while forging:\n\n<b>Stop for Vastium:</b> Always stops if you roll a Vastium piece, even if it is a downgrade.\n\n<b>Stat Matching:</b> With this enabled, the forge will continue to work until an upgrade has the exact same stat types as your equipped piece of gear.\n\nQuality is represented by this icon: <sprite=206>\n\nThis is where you craft gear and choose the best stats for your build. \nRight now there are 8 stats that can be rolled on gear with each piece guaranteeing a specific one.\n\n<sprite=198> = Damage.\n<sprite=200> = Attack Speed.\n<sprite=199> = Crit Chance.\n<sprite=205> = Crit Damage.  \n\n<sprite=202> = Health.\n<sprite=203> = Regen.\n<sprite=201> = Defense.\n<sprite=204> = Movement.\n\n<sprite=192> = Upgrade.\n<sprite=193> = Downgrade. \n<sprite=194> = No change.\n<sprite=195> Stat is not on new item.\n<sprite=196> Stat is not on old item.\n\n<b>Weapon</b> | Guarantees <sprite=198>\n<b>Helmet</b> | Guarantees <sprite=202>\n<b>Chest</b> | Guarantees <sprite=201>\n<b>Boots</b> | Guarantees <sprite=204> which is exclusive to this slot.\n\nGear is automatically salvaged when you craft a new piece, select a different slot, or close the game.\n\nDepending on rarity you can receive up to 5 stats on a piece of gear. There are plans to add additional stats to gear in the future!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9824133185945600
    m_Localized: "Hey guys Dev here. \n\nIf you want your names in the enemy name random pool of names then please jump into discord and ask in the EoV Chat :)\n\n\u2022 I am considering moving task unlocks to the milestone system. Quests would then provide skill xp instead of task unlocks! Let me know your thoughts."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9898115700506624
    m_Localized: "<b>Changes</b>\n\u2022 Added two new quests. For the Jam! & Gilliver's Travels.\n\u2022 Improved intro message.\n\u2022 Fixed level up alerts showing lower values than you had.\n\u2022 Removed the Forge stats Quality Equipped block.\n\u2022 Pinned quests now say \"Ready to turn in\" rather than \"Complete.\n\u2022 Added an overlay when loading a map.\n\u2022 Added a new Mix All Button.\n<b>Backend</b>\n\u2022 Updated A* to a newer version."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12027031164698624
    m_Localized: 'The Cauldron converts selected food into stew. You choose how much to mix; stew gained depends on the food''s authored value and the quantity. Taste stew to receive cards using Eva''s displayed reward weights.


      Resource cards improve genuine gathering, enemy drops and town crop harvests for the matching resource. Their copy thresholds are 1, 25, 75, 200, 750, 1500, 3500 and 10000; yield bonuses are 1%, 2%, 3%, 5%, 7%, 10%, 15% and 20%.


      A resource category uses the lowest card tier among its unlocked resources. Unowned cards count as tier zero. Category tiers 1 through 8 add 2%, 5%, 10%, 15%, 20%, 30%, 40% and 50% yield to that category. Card and category bonuses add together, up to 70%. Rewards, seeds, refunds and conversions do not receive these bonuses.


      These card tiers are separate from resource rarity. Existing buff-card cooldown and power benefits remain unchanged. Complete all available resource and buff collections to unlock Eternal Boons.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18915029441462272
    m_Localized: 'Items have a low chance of tiering up each time you collect them. Town farm harvests do not roll resource tier upgrades.

      Each tier above the first grants you bonus resources each time you collect it in the future.


      I''m a bit loathe to share this information with you but here you go - Orin...


      Tier | Bonus | Chance

      <b>Tier 1</b> - 0%\tBase

      <b>Tier 2</b> - 10%\t1 /1,000

      <b>Tier 3</b> - 20%\t1 / 5,000

      <b>Tier 4</b> - 30%\t1 / 10,000

      <b>Tier 5</b> - 50%\t1 / 50,000

      <b>Tier 6</b> - 75%\t1 / 100,000

      <b>Tier 7</b> - 100%\t1 / 250,000

      <b>Tier 8</b> - 150%\t1 / 1,000,000'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25772880722018304
    m_Localized: English (en)
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255181967360
    m_Localized: Adventures & Maps
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299008
    m_Localized: "<b>Start:</b> Adventure \u2192 select a map.\n\nYour character travels between tasks and gathers resources automatically. Each map has different resources.\n\n<b>Map information:</b> Statistics \u2192 General \u2192 select a map. Discovered resources are shown there. Locked maps show where to learn more."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299009
    m_Localized: Farming tasks appear only in Farmlands. Quests and NPC encounters unlock other routes.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299010
    m_Localized: Tasks & Skills
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299011
    m_Localized: "Tasks award resources and skill XP.\n\n<b>Skill bonuses and unlocks:</b> Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 select a skill.\n\n<b>Task chances:</b> Statistics \u2192 Tasks. Adjust a task's weight to change how often it appears among eligible tasks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299012
    m_Localized: "Task weights do not unlock tasks or change which maps they appear on. Map, distance, and progression still apply.\n\nCombat levels unlock higher core and crystal tiers. Required levels are listed under Skills \u2192 Combat."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299013
    m_Localized: Quests
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299014
    m_Localized: '<b>Open:</b> Quests.


      Accept a quest, complete its requirements, then turn it in while in town. Resource hand-ins spend the requested items.


      Tracked quests appear on your HUD. Untracked quests remain in the quest list.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299015
    m_Localized: 'A quest can require resources, enemy kills, an NPC meeting, or a guided interaction. Meeting its requirements makes it ready to turn in; rewards are claimed at turn-in.


      Quests cannot be turned in during an adventure.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299016
    m_Localized: Inventory & Equipment
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299017
    m_Localized: "<b>Open:</b> Hub \u2192 Inventory.\n\nSelect an equipped slot to inspect its bonuses. Total equipment bonuses combine all equipped items.\n\nCompare stat values when replacing equipment. Higher rarity does not guarantee a better item.\n\n<b>Current combat stats:</b> in-run HUD \u2192 Stats."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299018
    m_Localized: Discovered resources appear first, followed by undiscovered resources. Each group keeps your chosen sort order.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299019
    m_Localized: Combat
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299020
    m_Localized: "Your character fights enemies automatically, then returns to their task.\n\n<b>Current stats:</b> in-run HUD \u2192 Stats.\n<b>Enemy stats and kill bonuses:</b> Statistics \u2192 Enemies."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299021
    m_Localized: "<b>Defense:</b> with default tuning, damage taken = incoming damage \xD7 25 \xF7 (defense + 25). Negative defense is treated as zero.\n\nRepeated kills against an enemy grant bonus damage against that enemy. Its Statistics entry shows the bonus and next milestone."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299022
    m_Localized: Reaping & Returning
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299023
    m_Localized: "Carl reaps your character at the map's limit. The run ends; gathered resources and skill progress are kept.\n\nReturn to town to turn in quests. The Run Summary lists your gains and progress.\n\n<b>Map limits:</b> Statistics \u2192 General \u2192 select a map."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299024
    m_Localized: Reaping at the limit increases distance by 1% on River, Woods, and Mines. Farmlands gives no increase. Spooky uses a kill limit instead of distance. Some quests also increase your reach.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299025
    m_Localized: Retreat Bonus
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299026
    m_Localized: '<b>Return:</b> use the return-to-town control during a run.


      Each kill adds 2% to your retreat resource bonus. The return control shows the current bonus.


      A return requested during combat is queued until the fight ends.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299027
    m_Localized: The retreat bonus is based on kills earned during the current run. Reaping and retreating are different ways to end a run.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299028
    m_Localized: Forge
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299029
    m_Localized: "<b>Open:</b> Townsfolk \u2192 Forge, after meeting Ivan.\n\n<b>1. Smelt ingots</b> from the required materials.\n<b>2. Select a core.</b> It sets rarity odds and material costs.\n<b>3. Select a slot and Craft.</b> Each craft spends ingots and one core.\n<b>4. Compare the result.</b> Choose Equip to replace your current item.\n\nOutside Ivan's lesson, crafting for an empty slot equips the result automatically."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299030
    m_Localized: "<b>Salvage</b>\nAn unused result is salvaged when you craft again or switch slots. Review it before continuing.\n\n<b>Automation \u2014 Forge mastery level 3</b>\nCraft Until Upgrade repeats crafting and spends materials each time.\nStop for Vastium stops on a Vastium result, even if it is a downgrade.\nStat Matching requires an upgrade to match your equipped item's affix types before stopping for that upgrade.\n\n<b>Core and crystal unlocks:</b> Hub \u2192 Skills \u2192 Combat."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299031
    m_Localized: Buffs
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299032
    m_Localized: "<b>Open:</b> Hub \u2192 Buffs.\n\nBuffs provide temporary bonuses. Check the effect, cost, and duration before activating one. Buffs expire when their duration ends or you return to town.\n\nComplete a slot's required quest to unlock autocasting. Toggle autocasting from that slot."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299033
    m_Localized: Eva's Cauldron provides buff cards that improve power and cooldowns.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299034
    m_Localized: Cauldron
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299035
    m_Localized: "<b>Open:</b> Townsfolk \u2192 Cauldron.\n\nMix food into stew, then taste the stew to receive cards. Check the displayed reward chances before tasting.\n\nResource cards increase matching resource yield. Buff cards improve buffs. Card levels are separate from resource rarity tiers."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299036
    m_Localized: 'A category uses the lowest card tier among its unlocked resources; unowned cards count as tier zero.


      Resource-card and category bonuses add together, up to 70%. They apply to gathering, enemy drops, and town crop harvests. Rewards, seeds, refunds, and conversions do not receive them.


      Complete all available resource and buff collections to unlock Eternal Boons.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299037
    m_Localized: Echoes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299038
    m_Localized: "Echoes are temporary copies of your character that gather resources or fight enemies.\n\nOrin's realms are connected. Spikes in temporal energy let Echoes of your past cross between them to help you. Helping the townsfolk earns you the power to summon Echoes at will.\n\nSkill milestone Echoes seek tasks belonging to that skill. Check Skills \u2192 Milestones or the summoning buff for its effects."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299039
    m_Localized: An Echo with both task and combat abilities prioritizes tasks and fights when engaged.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299040
    m_Localized: Resource Tiers
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299041
    m_Localized: 'Gathering can raise a resource''s rarity tier. Higher tiers permanently increase future yield for that resource.


      Town crop harvests use your current tier bonus but do not roll upgrades.


      Resource tiers, equipment rarity, and Cauldron card levels are separate systems.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164580255232299042
    m_Localized: Upgrade chances are per eligible collection at the previous tier. Tier 1 is the starting tier.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
