  - m_Id: 164588427254829056
    m_Localized: '<b>Farmlands</b>

      Gather crops here. Farming tasks do not appear on other maps. Carl''s distance limit does not increase when you are reaped in Farmlands.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160704
    m_Localized: "<b>Farming</b>\nHarvest crop patches in Farmlands to gain crops and Farming XP. These adventure tasks are separate from planting crops in town. Check Skills \u2192 Farming for bonuses and unlocks."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160705
    m_Localized: "<b>Fishing</b>\nGill provides your first rod. Fishing tasks catch fish and award Fishing XP. Check Statistics \u2192 General for a map's discovered resources, and Skills \u2192 Fishing for progression."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160706
    m_Localized: "<b>Mining</b>\nMining tasks provide ores and Mining XP. Smelt ores into ingots at the Forge to craft equipment. Check Skills \u2192 Mining for ore unlock levels."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160707
    m_Localized: "<b>Woodcutting</b>\nWoodcutting tasks provide wood resources and Woodcutting XP. Follow Barkley's quests to progress into the Woods. Check Skills \u2192 Woodcutting for unlocks and Statistics \u2192 Tasks to adjust eligible task chances."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427305160708
    m_Localized: '<b>Ready to turn in</b>

      The star marks a quest whose requirements are met. Return to town and select Turn In to claim its reward. Resource hand-ins spend the listed items.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355008
    m_Localized: '<b>Weapon</b>

      Crafted weapons guarantee damage. Compare the other rolled stats before replacing your current weapon.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355009
    m_Localized: '<b>Helmet</b>

      Crafted helmets guarantee health. Other rolled stats can improve offense, defense, or recovery.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355010
    m_Localized: '<b>Chest</b>

      Crafted chest pieces guarantee defense. Defense reduces incoming damage with diminishing returns.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355011
    m_Localized: '<b>Boots</b>

      Crafted boots guarantee movement, which increases travel speed. Movement rolls are exclusive to this slot.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355012
    m_Localized: '<b>Damage</b>

      Determines damage dealt per hit before enemy defense and other modifiers. Attack speed controls how often you hit; critical chance and critical damage affect critical hits. View current values in the in-run Stats panel.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355013
    m_Localized: '<b>Defense</b>

      Reduces incoming damage. At 25 defense you take half damage; at 75 defense you take one quarter. Defense does not prevent damage completely. The formula is in Reference.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355014
    m_Localized: '<b>Health</b>

      Your character dies when health reaches zero. Equipment can increase maximum health; regeneration restores health over time. Check the health bar and current Stats during a run.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355015
    m_Localized: '<b>Carl</b>

      Carl ends the run at the map''s limit. You keep gathered resources and skill progress. River, Woods, and Mines gain 1% distance when you are reaped at the limit; Farmlands does not. Spooky uses kills instead of distance.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355016
    m_Localized: '<b>Ingots</b>

      Smelt the materials shown by the ingot control. The selected core determines the ingot type and quantity required for a craft. Smelting creates materials; it does not create equipment.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355017
    m_Localized: '<b>Cores</b>

      Each craft consumes one core. The selected core determines rarity odds and material costs. Combat levels unlock higher core tiers; upgrade cores using the Forge''s conversion controls.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355018
    m_Localized: '<b>Sword</b>

      Select Weapon, then Craft. Weapons guarantee a damage stat. Review the rolled bonuses and choose Equip to replace your current weapon. An unused result is salvaged when you craft again or switch slots.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355019
    m_Localized: "<b>Resource Doubler</b>\nA temporary resource-gathering buff. Check its displayed effect, cost, and duration in Hub \u2192 Buffs. Eligible slots can autocast after their required quests are completed."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355020
    m_Localized: "<b>Task Speed</b>\nA temporary buff that speeds up task completion. Manage its slot and autocasting in Hub \u2192 Buffs. Buffs end when their duration expires or you return to town."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355021
    m_Localized: '<b>Cauldron</b>

      Choose food and a quantity to mix into stew. Taste stew to receive cards using the displayed reward chances. Resource cards improve matching resource yield; buff cards improve buffs. Reference lists resource-card and category thresholds.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355022
    m_Localized: '<b>Task Echo</b>

      Gathers resources without attacking or attracting enemies. Skill milestone Echoes seek tasks for that skill. The summoning buff or milestone specifies the Echo''s duration and abilities.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164588427309355023
    m_Localized: '<b>Combat Echo</b>

      Seeks and fights enemies. Combat-only Echoes do not gather resources. An Echo with both task and combat abilities prioritizes tasks and fights when engaged.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164590655340417024
    m_Localized: Patch Notes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164590655378165760
    m_Localized: "<b>Current development changes</b>\n\n<b>Opening and progression</b>\n\u2022 Reworked the opening quests and NPC introductions.\n\u2022 Gill leads players to the River; Barkley leads them toward the Woods.\n\u2022 Gill rewards Old Boots. Ivan supplies materials and teaches players to forge and equip their first sword.\n\u2022 Menus and tutorials appear as their systems become relevant.\n\u2022 Quests can only be turned in while in town.\n\n<b>Interface</b>\n\u2022 Redesigned the Run Summary and added a compact in-run Stats panel.\n\u2022 Inventory now shows equipped items and equipment bonuses.\n\u2022 Added drag scrolling throughout the interface.\n\u2022 Rebuilt the Library with topic navigation, reference tables, and selectable icon explanations.\n\n<b>Gameplay and fixes</b>\n\u2022 Reduced task density on the first Farmlands adventure.\n\u2022 Farming tasks appear only in Farmlands.\n\u2022 Core and crystal tiers unlock through Combat levels.\n\u2022 Fixed enemy health-bar overlays and fishing animation issues.\n\u2022 Removed leaderboards.\n\nSelect Reference for earlier patch notes."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 164590655378165761
    m_Localized: "<b>Earlier patch notes</b>\n\n\u2022 Added For the Jam! and Gilliver's Travels.\n\u2022 Improved the introduction message.\n\u2022 Fixed level-up alerts showing lower values than expected.\n\u2022 Removed the Forge's Quality Equipped block.\n\u2022 Pinned quests show Ready to turn in instead of Complete.\n\u2022 Added a loading overlay when changing maps.\n\u2022 Added the Cauldron's Mix All button.\n\u2022 Updated the pathfinding package."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
